WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.921
<i>♪ It seems today that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.922 --> 00:07.965
<i>♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪</i>

00:07.966 --> 00:11.802
<i>♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.803 --> 00:14.847
<i>♪ On which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.848 --> 00:18.309
<i>♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.310 --> 00:21.604
<i>♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.605 --> 00:23.189
<i>♪ All the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.190 --> 00:25.024
<i>♪ Laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:25.025 --> 00:30.322
<i>♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:34.743 --> 00:37.411
<i>Coming this winter: actors
who don't look familiar</i>

00:37.412 --> 00:39.580
<i>in shows you're pretty sure
you've never heard of</i>

00:39.581 --> 00:42.083
<i>on networks you've
definitely never heard of.</i>

00:42.084 --> 00:45.253
<i>First, it's The Marriage Man
on Geego Audience Prime Plus.</i>

00:45.254 --> 00:47.088
<i>Then Frenemy on Goldstar.</i>

00:47.089 --> 00:49.840
<i>And don't forget The
J. Tory Hampton Show on Traxx.</i>

00:49.841 --> 00:51.509
<i>Lump Monkeys on Forge.</i>

00:51.510 --> 00:53.511
<i>Comeuppance on LFR America.</i>

00:53.512 --> 00:55.513
<i>Tattle Babies on Blitz Kids.</i>

00:55.514 --> 00:57.807
<i>And Snapchatters on Perspire.</i>

00:57.808 --> 00:59.976
<i>Who's watching them? Probably no one.</i>

00:59.977 --> 01:01.310
<i>Are they comedies or dramas?</i>

01:01.311 --> 01:02.687
<i>We're not even sure.</i>

01:02.688 --> 01:03.980
<i>Turn your office watercooler</i>

01:03.981 --> 01:05.856
<i>into a modern-day Tower of Babel.</i>

01:05.857 --> 01:07.441
<i>- The Marriage Man!
- Lump Monkeys!</i>

01:07.442 --> 01:09.318
<i>- The J. Tory Hampton Show!
- Lump Monkeys!</i>

01:10.529 --> 01:12.113
<i>Gay Paree!</i>

01:12.114 --> 01:14.156
<i>TV: what a mess.</i>

01:14.157 --> 01:15.538
Hi, everybody.

01:15.539 --> 01:18.703
You know how I've been dieting
like a maniac the last couple weeks?

01:18.704 --> 01:20.997
Aw, damn it, that means
we're having people over.

01:20.998 --> 01:23.459
We're having people over!

01:23.460 --> 01:25.334
I just got off the phone with my mom,

01:25.335 --> 01:27.962
and all the Pewterschmidts are
coming here for Thanksgiving.

01:27.963 --> 01:30.339
I can't believe
you invited the whole family.

01:30.340 --> 01:31.966
You know I hate big Thanksgivings.

01:31.967 --> 01:33.718
Don't worry, Peter, it's gonna be fun.

01:33.719 --> 01:35.678
And I can handle
most of the prep myself.

01:35.679 --> 01:37.471
I just need you to go to the market

01:37.472 --> 01:39.098
and get some extra napkins.

01:39.099 --> 01:42.018
- That's not so bad.
- Oh. Pick up some wine for the adults.

01:42.019 --> 01:43.184
I can do that.

01:43.185 --> 01:45.396
A-And put the extra leaf
in the dining room table.

01:47.399 --> 01:49.483
Oh, stop it. It's so simple.

01:49.484 --> 01:51.902
Yeah, right. That table
ain't been opened in five years.

01:51.903 --> 01:54.405
It'll be fine. Just don't drink
while you do it.

01:54.406 --> 01:57.742
And for God's sake, don't lose
your temper with Chris.

01:57.743 --> 02:00.369
All right, one, two, three.

02:00.370 --> 02:01.579
Hup!

02:02.873 --> 02:04.182
One more time.

02:04.183 --> 02:05.207
Hup!

02:06.209 --> 02:07.585
Okay, all right, bend the knees.

02:07.586 --> 02:09.045
Let's give it a good pull.

02:09.046 --> 02:10.421
Hup!

02:10.422 --> 02:12.256
Yeah, I think one side is stuck.

02:12.257 --> 02:14.383
Do you, son? Okay, on three.

02:14.384 --> 02:16.093
One, two, three.

02:16.094 --> 02:17.345
Hup!

02:17.346 --> 02:19.930
Hup! Hup!

02:19.931 --> 02:22.099
Hup! Hup! Hup!

02:24.227 --> 02:26.062
I think it's still stuck.

02:26.063 --> 02:27.521
Oh, is that right?

02:27.522 --> 02:28.898
Lot of narration.

02:28.899 --> 02:31.167
It's like opening a table
with Ken Burns.

02:32.069 --> 02:34.195
Um, why don't you go easy on that stuff?

02:34.196 --> 02:36.447
This "stuff" is
the only thing stopping you

02:36.448 --> 02:38.616
from getting
so karate-chopped right now.

02:38.617 --> 02:40.284
Okay, big pull, on three.

02:40.285 --> 02:41.952
All right, one, two, three.

02:41.953 --> 02:43.079
Hup!

02:43.080 --> 02:45.122
It's this one side, it's just stuck.

02:45.123 --> 02:46.166
I know it's stuck!

02:46.167 --> 02:47.792
Everyone sees it's stuck!

02:47.793 --> 02:50.127
Are there voices you're hearing
shouting, "It's not stuck"?

02:50.128 --> 02:51.921
'Cause if you hear any argument

02:51.922 --> 02:53.964
from anybody who says it isn't stuck,

02:53.965 --> 02:57.385
you send them to me, and I will
so karate-chop them in the face!

02:57.386 --> 02:59.303
Got it?!

02:59.304 --> 03:01.097
I'm not sure that that's...

03:01.098 --> 03:03.974
What?! What aren't you sure about?

03:03.975 --> 03:04.975
Hup!

03:04.976 --> 03:07.561
Hup! Hup! Hup!

03:07.562 --> 03:09.897
Hey, Chris. Table looks stuck.

03:09.898 --> 03:13.184
Oh, really?
"Sky blue," says star witness.

03:18.907 --> 03:21.117
You know what's crazy
about this time of year?

03:21.118 --> 03:23.119
Everything is pumpkin spice.

03:23.120 --> 03:25.538
We all follow your Twitter feed, Joe.

03:25.539 --> 03:27.748
God, Thanksgiving
is such a pain in the ass.

03:27.749 --> 03:29.413
I hate hosting.

03:29.414 --> 03:31.168
I hear you, Peter.
I hate Thanksgiving, too.

03:31.169 --> 03:34.296
Bonnie's sister is married
to a real show-off.

03:34.297 --> 03:37.341
Denise, Wendell, it's great to see you.

03:39.177 --> 03:41.429
- Wendell.
- Joseph.

03:41.430 --> 03:44.183
It's just Joe. I think you know that.

03:44.184 --> 03:46.142
My Thanksgiving's also a nightmare.

03:46.143 --> 03:49.854
Donna's cousins are two-thirds
of Tony! Toni! Ton├й!

03:49.855 --> 03:51.939
- Which ones?
- The "E" and the "I."

03:51.940 --> 03:53.691
Aw, no Tony with a "Y."

03:53.692 --> 03:54.859
That is correct.

03:54.860 --> 03:57.111
We lack the alpha Tony.

03:57.112 --> 03:59.196
Well, at least you guys
celebrate with your families.

03:59.197 --> 04:02.700
Last year I spent Thanksgiving
with my old blow-up sex dolls.

04:02.701 --> 04:04.197
Here you go, Carla.

04:04.198 --> 04:06.036
See? We can do other things together.

04:06.037 --> 04:08.038
How's the turkey? I made it myself.

04:08.039 --> 04:10.458
Oh, don't look so surprised.

04:11.710 --> 04:13.210
Ah. Someone's getting sleepy.

04:13.211 --> 04:14.378
Must be the tryptophan.

04:14.379 --> 04:16.046
I'll put a pot of coffee on.

04:16.047 --> 04:17.955
Janet, coffee? Carla, coffee?

04:17.956 --> 04:19.967
Dina, coffee? Sasha, coffee?

04:19.968 --> 04:21.677
Dad, coffee?

04:21.678 --> 04:24.430
I wish I had given you
more siblings, Glenn.

04:24.431 --> 04:26.640
You know, sometimes I envy
the guys in the town jail.

04:26.641 --> 04:28.476
They get a turkey dinner on Quahog

04:28.477 --> 04:31.060
and don't have the hassle
of hosting their families.

04:31.061 --> 04:32.730
Well, yeah, but they're in prison.

04:32.731 --> 04:35.954
Nah, jail isn't prison.
Prison is big and scary.

04:35.955 --> 04:38.724
Jail is just a sleeping deputy
with keys that can be grabbed

04:38.725 --> 04:41.945
by a long broom handle
or a mischievous dog.

04:41.946 --> 04:43.657
Do black people ever go to jail?

04:43.658 --> 04:45.534
No. They go to prison.

04:45.535 --> 04:48.078
Well, maybe going to jail
is what we should do.

04:48.079 --> 04:50.920
- Peter, that's ridiculous.
- H-H-Hear me out, hear me out.

04:50.921 --> 04:54.418
We'll commit a small crime
and get put in jail for a couple days.

04:54.419 --> 04:56.545
- That's insane!
- Peter, Peter, you're crazy!

04:56.546 --> 04:58.130
<i>- Ridiculous!
- Lump Monkeys!</i>

04:58.131 --> 05:00.341
<i>- Have you lost your mind?
- Lump Monkeys!</i>

05:00.342 --> 05:02.343
<i>All right, Joe,
there's chaos at the top.</i>

05:02.344 --> 05:04.386
<i>Time to step up and be the leader</i>

05:04.387 --> 05:06.347
<i>- of this group of friends.
- Lump Monkeys!</i>

05:06.348 --> 05:08.820
Guys, what if we all go to Vermont?

05:09.726 --> 05:12.103
Let's just do Peter's thing.

05:13.772 --> 05:15.606
Okay, if we want to get arrested,

05:15.607 --> 05:18.025
the best way to do it is
to get caught on the Ring app

05:18.026 --> 05:19.777
stealing people's packages.

05:44.052 --> 05:45.469
I forgot to steal the package.

05:45.470 --> 05:47.304
I think this is probably enough.

05:47.305 --> 05:50.307
I don't know exactly what this is,

05:50.308 --> 05:52.768
but this... this is crime.

05:52.769 --> 05:54.103
Swanson!

05:54.104 --> 05:56.564
Police Superintendent Chalmers.

05:56.565 --> 05:59.650
My brother is superintendent
of the schools in Springfield.

05:59.651 --> 06:02.486
Our parents divorced
when we were very young.

06:02.487 --> 06:04.488
I was raised entirely by our mother,

06:04.489 --> 06:05.739
he by our father.

06:05.740 --> 06:08.742
We've never met.
There's a lot of backstory.

06:08.743 --> 06:11.203
And you four are under arrest.

06:15.750 --> 06:17.543
I can't believe the plan worked.

06:17.544 --> 06:20.297
Here we are, the city jail.

06:22.714 --> 06:24.967
What's going on? Why aren't we stopping?

06:24.968 --> 06:27.344
You guys think you're the
first ones to have this idea?

06:27.345 --> 06:30.556
The jail's already full of dads
getting out of Thanksgiving.

06:30.557 --> 06:32.641
Well, if we're not going to Quahog jail,

06:32.642 --> 06:34.018
where are we going?

06:34.019 --> 06:36.186
The only place where
there's room for the weekend:

06:36.187 --> 06:37.647
the state penitentiary.

06:39.190 --> 06:41.442
You guys thinking what I'm thinking?

06:41.443 --> 06:44.028
Wacky mug shot montage.

06:50.702 --> 06:52.369
Hey, uh, are my friends coming?

06:52.370 --> 06:54.038
No, they're all calling lawyers.

06:54.039 --> 06:57.374
You used your one call on
this party photo booth guy.

06:57.375 --> 07:00.003
Eh, we'll see who has
more fun this weekend.

07:12.557 --> 07:14.224
Yeah, it just doesn't seem right.

07:14.225 --> 07:15.809
We're in here,
and everyone on Wall Street

07:15.810 --> 07:17.478
is free as a bird.

07:17.479 --> 07:20.814
Joe, now is not the time for
your bland political musings.

07:20.815 --> 07:23.525
This sucks. The courts are
closed for Thanksgiving,

07:23.526 --> 07:25.903
which means we can't even
go before a judge till Monday.

07:25.904 --> 07:27.696
That's five whole days here.

07:27.697 --> 07:29.531
What the hell are we gonna do?

07:29.532 --> 07:32.326
Well, if we're congress,
we'll do nothing.

07:32.327 --> 07:35.079
All right, that one was sharp.
Good job, Joe.

07:35.080 --> 07:37.373
And you know, maybe-maybe prison
won't be so bad.

07:37.374 --> 07:38.874
Maybe we just got to
make the best of it.

07:38.875 --> 07:40.292
Like those guys over there. Look.

07:40.293 --> 07:43.879
They're playing leapfrog.
No one's jumping, though.

07:43.880 --> 07:46.256
And that guy in the back
definitely has to get up higher.

07:46.257 --> 07:47.591
Who taught these guys how to play?

07:47.592 --> 07:48.967
Peter, please stop watching it.

07:48.968 --> 07:51.637
Guys, I think we're in trouble here.

07:51.638 --> 07:52.846
Come on, we're gonna be fine.

07:52.847 --> 07:54.765
Joe, you should be
more terrified than any of us.

07:54.766 --> 07:56.767
What if someone figures out
you're a cop?

07:56.768 --> 07:59.061
It's not gonna happen.
I spent years undercover.

07:59.062 --> 08:01.355
I'm a master of disguise.

08:01.356 --> 08:02.940
What? You're in a wheelchair.

08:02.941 --> 08:04.692
You can't disguise yourself as anything.

08:04.693 --> 08:07.194
<i>Is that so, Dad?</i>

08:07.195 --> 08:09.405
Chris? But that's impossible.

08:09.406 --> 08:11.532
I've seen Chris standing up many times.

08:11.533 --> 08:13.075
Have you?

08:13.076 --> 08:15.369
Hey, Chris, I got two tickets
for the Sox.

08:15.370 --> 08:18.247
- Want to go?
- You got it, Dad.

08:18.248 --> 08:20.207
Oh, charley horse.

08:20.208 --> 08:21.875
Oh, another charley horse, huh?

08:21.876 --> 08:23.252
Well, you sit tight, Chris.

08:23.253 --> 08:25.422
I can just take Joe's
brother-in-law Wendell.

08:26.214 --> 08:27.798
Christopher.

08:27.799 --> 08:31.428
It's just Chris. I think you know that.

08:36.391 --> 08:38.809
The conjugal visit room is being used.

08:38.810 --> 08:40.728
So, does your foot reach?

08:40.729 --> 08:42.896
Peter, enough. You ruined Thanksgiving.

08:42.897 --> 08:45.275
I have to host 20 people by myself.

08:46.276 --> 08:47.943
- You smoke now?
- Yeah.

08:47.944 --> 08:49.319
I have a husband in prison.

08:49.320 --> 08:51.197
That's who smokes, genius.

08:54.033 --> 08:57.119
Stewie, why do you look like
1976 Elton John?

08:57.120 --> 08:58.912
I'm trying to keep a low profile.

08:58.913 --> 09:00.789
You know that old sitcom premise

09:00.790 --> 09:02.750
where the kid has two dates to the prom?

09:02.751 --> 09:04.168
Well, I, um...

09:04.169 --> 09:07.796
I may sorta, kinda be engaged
to four prisoners.

09:07.797 --> 09:09.631
You're what? Stewie, that's crazy.

09:09.632 --> 09:11.425
Oh, relax, Brian,
I'm just humoring them.

09:11.426 --> 09:12.509
It's not serious.

09:12.510 --> 09:14.136
Stewie, don't forget,

09:14.137 --> 09:15.679
we're meeting DJs tomorrow.

09:15.680 --> 09:17.765
Sure thing, Clint.

09:17.766 --> 09:19.516
<i>His mother thinks it's her wedding.</i>

09:19.517 --> 09:20.809
But we'll see.

09:20.810 --> 09:22.352
How did you even meet these guys?

09:22.353 --> 09:24.104
Easily. They were my pen pals.

09:24.105 --> 09:25.647
You have prison pen pals?

09:25.648 --> 09:27.357
Yes. A lot of people write prisoners.

09:27.358 --> 09:29.693
Even Hollywood celebrity Kal Penn.

09:29.694 --> 09:31.320
Kal Penn writes a prisoner?

09:31.321 --> 09:33.280
Yeah. Ken. Lives in California.

09:33.281 --> 09:35.282
You've never heard of
Kal Penn's pen pal Ken

09:35.283 --> 09:36.492
in the Cal pen?

09:36.493 --> 09:38.202
How could I possibly
have heard of Kal Penn's

09:38.203 --> 09:39.453
pen pal Ken in the Cal pen?

09:39.454 --> 09:41.038
Through this song.

09:41.039 --> 09:43.457
<i>♪ Well, I do get a yen
every now and then ♪</i>

09:43.458 --> 09:45.459
<i>♪ To pick up a pen,
like my pal Kal Penn ♪</i>

09:45.460 --> 09:47.085
<i>♪ And a note I will send
every now and again ♪</i>

09:47.086 --> 09:49.588
<i>♪ To my pal Big Ben
who is locked in the pen ♪</i>

09:49.589 --> 09:51.381
<i>♪ 'Cause he beat up some men
and he got five to ten ♪</i>

09:51.382 --> 09:52.716
<i>♪ And he'll do it again ♪</i>

09:52.717 --> 09:53.717
<i>♪ Dah, dah, dah-dah-dah ♪</i>

09:53.718 --> 09:55.010
<i>♪ Kal Penn. ♪</i>

09:55.011 --> 09:57.054
- Who was that for?
- What are you talking about?

09:57.055 --> 09:58.597
Phil Spector's in this prison.

09:58.598 --> 10:01.892
Kid, I know talent and shooting
waitresses in the mouth,

10:01.893 --> 10:03.352
and you've got talent.

10:03.353 --> 10:04.982
We're gonna make a record.

10:19.202 --> 10:21.787
God, every crevice
of this prison is terrifying.

10:21.788 --> 10:23.205
Eh, it's not so bad.

10:23.206 --> 10:25.499
I made one-eye contact with Bill Cosby.

10:25.500 --> 10:27.334
Well, well, well.

10:27.335 --> 10:30.087
Three "wells" is never a good sign.

10:30.088 --> 10:32.838
- I think you guys have our lunches.
- Called it.

10:32.839 --> 10:34.675
Uh, sorry, sir.
We don't want any trouble.

10:34.676 --> 10:36.593
Yeah, we-we'll sit somewhere else.

10:36.594 --> 10:38.262
Come on, guys,
let's avoid confrontation.

10:38.263 --> 10:39.555
And whatever happens,

10:39.556 --> 10:41.598
let's make sure
we're not goaded into fights

10:41.599 --> 10:43.725
by simple playground taunts.

10:43.726 --> 10:46.563
Damn. I was hoping for chicken.

10:47.564 --> 10:51.233
Nobody calls me chicken.

10:51.234 --> 10:53.111
Peter, no!

10:55.446 --> 10:57.614
Aw, damn it, I lost a front tooth.

10:57.615 --> 10:59.700
Well, hopefully in the prison yearbook

10:59.701 --> 11:01.744
I'll just look
like a cute kindergartner.

11:04.914 --> 11:07.870
<i>Mad Dog, next time,
I'm asking</i>

11:07.871 --> 11:10.288
<i>for the "top bunk".</i>

11:10.289 --> 11:13.091
<i>LOL. Love Pete.</i>

11:17.427 --> 11:18.802
<i>I'm starving.</i>

11:18.803 --> 11:20.304
We haven't eaten since we got here.

11:20.305 --> 11:22.598
That's 'cause other prisoners
keep taking our meals.

11:22.599 --> 11:24.433
And God knows what else
they're gonna do to us.

11:24.434 --> 11:25.934
We have three more days here,

11:25.935 --> 11:27.603
and we're not gonna survive
three more minutes.

11:27.604 --> 11:29.062
That's 'cause you don't have a gang

11:29.063 --> 11:30.939
- to protect you.
- A gang?

11:30.940 --> 11:32.983
Yeah, when you're in a gang,
no one will mess with you.

11:32.984 --> 11:34.819
That's why everyone joins one.

11:34.820 --> 11:36.153
I used to be in a gang.

11:36.154 --> 11:38.238
It was called the Republican party.

11:38.239 --> 11:40.487
Our friend is very political.

11:40.488 --> 11:42.409
So, how do we get
into one of these gangs?

11:42.410 --> 11:44.494
Actually, you guys showed up
at the perfect time.

11:44.495 --> 11:46.330
Tomorrow is the start
of Prison Rush Week.

11:46.331 --> 11:48.290
Get in one, and you're home free.

11:48.291 --> 11:50.125
That's a great idea!

11:50.126 --> 11:53.546
Let's celebrate by pretentiously
analyzing some prison wine.

11:56.633 --> 12:00.469
Okay, I'm getting notes of, um...

12:00.470 --> 12:02.472
uh, well, feces.

12:12.813 --> 12:14.691
Man, getting in a gang

12:14.692 --> 12:16.276
is gonna be harder than I thought.

12:16.277 --> 12:18.070
Speak for yourself, Peter.

12:18.071 --> 12:19.863
What gang is this?

12:19.864 --> 12:21.198
We're the Not Cops.

12:21.199 --> 12:24.284
<i>We're all definitely not cops.</i>

12:24.285 --> 12:25.869
So you think firemen are cool?

12:25.870 --> 12:29.081
Firemen cook spaghetti.

12:29.082 --> 12:31.541
And I think y'all know who I joined.

12:31.542 --> 12:33.377
Are you now Kareem Abdul-Jableeveland?

12:33.378 --> 12:35.712
I am Kareem Abdul-Jableeveland.

12:35.713 --> 12:37.798
Hey, you know Muslims
can't drink alcohol, right?

12:37.799 --> 12:40.842
I am Cleveland "Hurricane" Carter.

12:40.843 --> 12:43.220
Well, Quagmire,
guess it's just you and me now.

12:43.221 --> 12:45.347
Sorry, Peter, I'm in MS-13.

12:45.348 --> 12:47.057
- What? How?
- It was easy.

12:47.058 --> 12:49.393
- I said I was loco.
- Loco!

12:49.394 --> 12:51.019
<i>- Si.
- Muy loco.</i>

12:51.020 --> 12:52.479
Well, I can be loco.

12:52.480 --> 12:54.398
I have a teardrop tattoo on my cheek.

12:54.399 --> 12:55.691
Where? I don't see it.

12:55.692 --> 12:56.901
Not-not that cheek.

12:58.027 --> 13:00.237
Peter, that's
an unwiped watermelon seed.

13:00.238 --> 13:02.823
- Loco?
- No. No loco.

13:02.824 --> 13:05.784
Hey, Peter,
is that your baby over there?

13:07.708 --> 13:10.247
We want fun. We want upbeat.
And for our dance,

13:10.248 --> 13:12.708
we want "You Belong with Me"
by Taylor Swift.

13:12.709 --> 13:15.210
Great, great. I also have
some more classic options,

13:15.211 --> 13:17.546
- like "At Last."
- Okay.

13:17.547 --> 13:21.258
So... so, what I need
is someone I can work with.

13:21.259 --> 13:23.845
Can you be that person?

13:28.682 --> 13:30.726
There you guys are.
I haven't seen you all day.

13:30.727 --> 13:33.020
<i>Me and the Not Cops
were watching Die Hard</i>

13:33.021 --> 13:34.771
<i>and not commenting</i>

13:34.772 --> 13:37.024
on the believability of the police work.

13:37.025 --> 13:39.568
Could John McClane
really foil a giant heist

13:39.569 --> 13:41.778
outside his jurisdiction,
then just walk away

13:41.779 --> 13:43.447
and do zero paperwork?

13:43.448 --> 13:45.782
We don't know or care,
'cause we're not cops.

13:45.783 --> 13:47.617
And I got my law degree.

13:47.618 --> 13:50.954
I am now Cleveland J. Roman J. Israel,

13:50.955 --> 13:53.540
and I will be wearing
wine-colored suits.

13:53.541 --> 13:55.917
- You look crazy.
- Well, in his defense,

13:55.918 --> 13:58.128
the movie was set in the '70s,
wasn't it?

13:58.129 --> 13:59.629
No, it's modern-day.

13:59.630 --> 14:01.133
Oh, my stars.

14:01.134 --> 14:03.133
All right, everyone, that's lanch.

14:03.134 --> 14:06.037
I mean, lunch. Sorry, it's my first day.

14:07.305 --> 14:08.466
This sucks.

14:08.467 --> 14:10.482
Everyone's eating lanch but me.

14:10.483 --> 14:12.141
I'm never gonna find a gang.

14:12.142 --> 14:14.311
Hey. You look like
you could use a friend.

14:14.312 --> 14:16.938
Well, let's just say in prison,

14:16.939 --> 14:19.232
this guy comes off.

14:19.233 --> 14:21.443
I meant my gang.
We're looking for members.

14:21.444 --> 14:23.779
- I-I bet you'd fit right in.
- Really?

14:23.780 --> 14:25.238
You only have to do one thing first.

14:25.239 --> 14:26.990
As the new white guy in prison,

14:26.991 --> 14:28.951
you have to shiv the new black guy.

14:31.954 --> 14:34.748
<i>Oh, you guys are that kind of gang.</i>

14:34.749 --> 14:36.204
This is prison.

14:36.205 --> 14:37.957
No one survives on their own.

14:37.958 --> 14:40.501
So it's either him or you.

14:40.502 --> 14:42.339
Man, I don't want to hurt Cleveland.

14:42.340 --> 14:44.925
But I don't want to die.
And it would be nice

14:44.926 --> 14:47.636
to have people to go
to Smash Mouth concerts with.

14:47.637 --> 14:49.638
Wait, you guys go
to Smash Mouth concerts, right?

14:49.639 --> 14:52.934
We're Nazis, Peter. We like Smash Mouth.

15:00.399 --> 15:02.359
Come on, there's got to be a way
you'll let me in the gang

15:02.360 --> 15:03.819
without shivving Cleveland.

15:03.820 --> 15:06.321
Ooh, ooh, I got an idea.
There was this prison movie,

15:06.322 --> 15:08.156
and-and there was this guy
who wanted to win over

15:08.157 --> 15:10.117
the other prisoners,
and you know what he did?

15:10.118 --> 15:12.786
He ate seven eggs. It was amazing.

15:12.787 --> 15:14.121
So, you bring me seven

15:14.122 --> 15:16.039
or some other reasonable amount
of eggs...

15:16.040 --> 15:17.624
Peter, I know it's 50 eggs.

15:17.625 --> 15:19.167
Ah, you're a film buff.

15:19.168 --> 15:22.879
Yeah. Before this, I was
in the USC directors program.

15:22.880 --> 15:24.214
Well, if you can call it that.

15:24.215 --> 15:25.841
You think you're learning about film,

15:25.842 --> 15:28.635
but, really, you're getting
a degree in politics.

15:28.636 --> 15:30.387
I know,
everything is so political.

15:30.388 --> 15:32.722
<i>So political. Best advice I ever got:</i>

15:32.723 --> 15:35.016
whatever business you think you work in,

15:35.017 --> 15:36.309
you really work in sales.

15:36.310 --> 15:38.311
Because you're always selling yourself.

15:38.312 --> 15:40.313
Yeah, wow, that is... that is good.

15:40.314 --> 15:42.899
- You are smart.
- Well, I didn't say it.

15:42.900 --> 15:44.401
- I'm just repeating it.
- Well, still,

15:44.402 --> 15:45.861
y-you recognized its value.

15:45.862 --> 15:47.655
That-That's not nothing.

15:50.658 --> 15:52.742
Well, we're so happy you're all here.

15:52.743 --> 15:54.411
We thought it might be fun

15:54.412 --> 15:57.247
to kick things off
with a game of Heads Up!

15:57.248 --> 15:58.915
- Daddy, do you want to start?
- No.

15:58.916 --> 16:00.750
You just hold this up to your head,

16:00.751 --> 16:03.920
and then we're gonna give you
clues to help you guess it.

16:03.921 --> 16:05.672
I only like games with sticks.

16:05.673 --> 16:07.174
Okay, ready?

16:07.175 --> 16:08.634
Go.

16:10.428 --> 16:11.970
Okay. It's a show.

16:11.971 --> 16:13.054
<i>Annie Get Your Gun.</i>

16:13.055 --> 16:14.181
No, it's on TV.

16:14.182 --> 16:16.707
<i>Oh. Poirot?</i>

16:16.708 --> 16:18.521
What is that? I've never heard of that.

16:18.522 --> 16:21.104
Uh, it's a Belgian detective on PBS.

16:21.105 --> 16:22.480
We just love it.

16:22.481 --> 16:25.567
It's about seven castaways.
There's a professor

16:25.568 --> 16:27.736
a-and a millionaire a-and a movie star.

16:27.737 --> 16:28.737
<i>- Poirot!
- No.</i>

16:28.738 --> 16:30.197
<i>We already said it's not Poirot.</i>

16:30.198 --> 16:32.532
It's about people who took
a three-hour tour.

16:32.533 --> 16:34.117
No, it's not.
It's about a Belgian detective.

16:34.118 --> 16:35.368
It's on PBS.

16:35.369 --> 16:38.205
The title character is played
by Bob Denver.

16:38.206 --> 16:40.707
- It's pronounced "David Suchet."
- Who's that?

16:40.708 --> 16:43.710
<i>- I'm gonna guess Poirot.
- It's not Poirot!</i>

16:43.711 --> 16:45.338
Damn it, just pass!

16:48.090 --> 16:49.424
Okay, this is a movie...

16:49.425 --> 16:51.301
<i>Roman J. Israel, Esq.</i>

16:51.302 --> 16:52.553
Yay!

17:05.483 --> 17:07.317
Come on, Peter, it's him or you.

17:07.318 --> 17:09.402
And-and he's not so great.

17:09.403 --> 17:10.737
Don't forget, he's the one who told you

17:10.738 --> 17:12.489
<i>all those Schoolhouse Rock! Spoilers.</i>

17:12.490 --> 17:14.574
I had no idea
that bill would become a law.

17:14.575 --> 17:16.117
Sorry, Peter.

17:16.118 --> 17:17.577
My gang said I wasn't really loco

17:17.578 --> 17:18.995
unless I shivved someone,

17:18.996 --> 17:21.748
and you're the one guy
without gang protection, so...

17:21.749 --> 17:23.291
Sorry, Quagmire.

17:23.292 --> 17:25.961
As a Not Cop, I have to shiv
a guy in the Latin gang

17:25.962 --> 17:28.171
and then blame it on Cleve...

17:28.172 --> 17:30.131
No one made me do this.

17:30.132 --> 17:33.052
I'm just sick of your overt racism.

17:35.805 --> 17:37.305
Guys, guys, stop.

17:37.306 --> 17:39.015
Stop. Look at us.

17:39.016 --> 17:41.518
We're shivving each other
on Thanksgiving.

17:41.519 --> 17:43.353
Oh, wait, no one shivved Cleveland.

17:44.522 --> 17:46.189
But what are we doing?

17:46.190 --> 17:47.440
What are all of us doing?

17:47.441 --> 17:49.651
Fighting in here amongst ourselves

17:49.652 --> 17:51.987
while Brooks is out there
waiting for all of us,

17:51.988 --> 17:53.154
bagging groceries,

17:53.155 --> 17:55.448
adapting to this new world seamlessly...

17:55.449 --> 17:56.783
Brooks hung himself.

17:56.784 --> 17:58.159
Oh, my stars.

17:58.160 --> 17:59.703
The point is, in life,

17:59.704 --> 18:02.539
you need to be thankful
for what you have.

18:02.540 --> 18:05.744
I wasn't, and it got me in here.

18:05.745 --> 18:09.655
I let down my family,
especially my wife.

18:09.656 --> 18:12.470
I just wish she was here
so I could tell her I'm sorry.

18:12.471 --> 18:14.077
I am here, Peter.

18:14.078 --> 18:16.511
Not now, prison ladyboy
who talks like my wife

18:16.512 --> 18:17.887
to please me sexually.

18:17.888 --> 18:19.890
No, Peter, we're here.

18:21.390 --> 18:23.737
Lois! What are you doing here?

18:23.738 --> 18:25.747
I thought you were having
Thanksgiving with your parents.

18:25.748 --> 18:27.897
Chris got caught
watching cousin Katie pee,

18:27.898 --> 18:29.482
so that kind of ended things.

18:29.483 --> 18:31.401
Well, I wanted to get caught. That's...

18:31.402 --> 18:33.153
It's part of it.

18:33.154 --> 18:36.364
And the truth is, Peter,
we're not a family without you.

18:36.365 --> 18:38.189
Can you ever forgive me?

18:38.190 --> 18:40.491
Of course I can, Peter.

18:40.492 --> 18:43.413
- Hi, Peter.
- Who's your little friend?

18:43.414 --> 18:44.748
Not now, Prison Lois.

18:44.749 --> 18:46.457
So it's over?

18:46.458 --> 18:48.002
And what was Venice?

18:48.003 --> 18:49.744
Same thing it always was, babe:

18:49.745 --> 18:51.921
a dream we both wanted to believe.

18:54.928 --> 18:57.969
- Peter, who was that?
- Not now, Front-Sex Lois.

18:57.970 --> 19:00.555
The important thing is,
my days of selfishness

19:00.556 --> 19:02.776
and red-wig twinks are over.

19:02.777 --> 19:04.893
I'm ready to come home with you.

19:04.894 --> 19:06.995
But, Peter,
you're in here till next week.

19:06.996 --> 19:08.772
Not anymore.

19:08.773 --> 19:10.451
Hi, I'm the warden

19:10.452 --> 19:12.275
and definitely not a psychotic prisoner

19:12.276 --> 19:14.844
who just stabbed the warden
and stole his clothes.

19:14.845 --> 19:17.072
Shh, shh!
Everyone, the warden's talking.

19:17.073 --> 19:19.282
<i>By the rules of prison
and The Love Boat,</i>

19:19.283 --> 19:20.784
you've made up,

19:20.785 --> 19:24.544
which means you get to leave
wiser and happier.

19:35.153 --> 19:36.853
I love you, Lois.

19:36.854 --> 19:38.386
I love you, Peter.

19:41.806 --> 19:44.791
Hey, Lois, one day, let's go to Venice.

19:44.792 --> 19:48.104
- You promise?
- I said it, didn't I?

19:49.145 --> 19:50.676
Donna!

19:50.677 --> 19:52.774
- Bonnie!
- Sex doll!

19:52.775 --> 19:55.819
Oh, yeah!

19:55.820 --> 19:58.614
All right, guys, settle down.

20:04.829 --> 20:07.080
Well, we're certainly glad
to have you home, Peter,

20:07.081 --> 20:08.623
but I hope you learned your lesson.

20:08.624 --> 20:10.785
I learned a hard lesson, Lois.

20:10.786 --> 20:12.253
But it's not all bad.

20:12.254 --> 20:14.087
I got to make a license plate
for our car

20:14.088 --> 20:17.019
- that says "butthole."
- Isn't that too many letters?

20:17.020 --> 20:19.335
Excellent question, Chris,
and yes, it is.

20:19.336 --> 20:22.011
But I took off a "T"
and the "E" at the end.

20:22.012 --> 20:23.732
I felt that was the right way to go.

20:23.733 --> 20:25.724
Trust me, people will get it.

20:27.139 --> 20:28.560
What's buthol?

20:28.561 --> 20:30.687
- That's not how you say it.
- Yeah, I've heard of buthol.

20:30.688 --> 20:32.355
It's some kind of alternative fuel.

20:32.356 --> 20:34.732
You're ruining a smart joke.

20:34.733 --> 20:36.192
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

20:36.193 --> 20:38.736
<i>please welcome, for the first time,</i>

20:38.737 --> 20:40.780
Mr. and Mrs. Clint Beltran!

20:44.827 --> 20:47.913
<i>♪ At last... ♪</i>

20:49.707 --> 20:50.874
Hey!

20:50.875 --> 20:52.501
You were right.

20:52.502 --> 20:54.498
<i>♪ My love ♪</i>

20:54.499 --> 20:57.006
<i>♪ Has come along. ♪</i>